Then write temp file in `filepath.Dir(target)` and rename to `target`. Permissions: os.Stat(target) — existing code stats `path`, which follows symlinks, so mode is already the target's mode. Good.

But wait — the dangling-symlink case must be rejected even before first-registration logic. Where does the rejection happen? Flow in main.go: `Load(path)` → dangling symlink → os.ReadFile returns ENOENT → existed=false, empty registry. Then Register creates → Save(path). In Save, Lstat shows symlink, EvalSymlinks fails (target doesn't exist) → error. Then main.go does `os.Remove(*registryPath)` because !existed — that would delete the symlink! Requirement says "不能…覆盖原链接" — the link must remain. Hmm: "应明确拒绝本次操作，错误说明用户传入的登记路径及具体原因，不能按首次登记处理、创建目标文件或覆盖原链接". So we must not remove the link.

So better to reject earlier — at Load time. If Load gets ENOENT but the path is a dangling symlink, return an error instead of existed=false. That way main.go's `os.Remove` cleanup never triggers (Load error returns before Save).

Actually the cleanup `os.Remove(*registryPath)` on save failure when !existed: with symlink handling in Save, if Save fails after rename... rename to target means link path never gets a partial file. The remove of link path would remove the symlink — bad. But if Load rejects dangling links, the only symlink case reaching Save is a valid link to an existing file, where existed=true, so no remove. Good.

